# cos/spec/check-catalogue.spec — every check Nexus can run on code, a component, a boundary or a running system, found by
# comparing the primitives and invariants of many domains. Structured so Nexus can load it (one entry = one check), not prose.
spec:
  meta:
    name:      check-catalogue
    version:   1.0.0
    date:      2026-10-13
    owner:     "cos (the test env, the torture chamber's stations, the lab) · cortex (RAID's gates) · diagnostic · intelligence · idearium (a repo's Debug tab)"
    status:    "CATALOGUED 2026-10-13 — a list to build from, not a list of what is built. `exists:` names the code that already does an entry (read in source, not run); everything else is OPEN."
    companions: "cos/spec/qa-catalog.spec (the 81-method survey, by family, with where each applies) · cos/spec/torture-chamber.spec (stations: { id, family, needs[], run, verdict }) · cos/spec/lab.spec (end-states and their checks) · docs/2026-10-12-request-spine-phasemap.spec RQ1 (the verifier library), RQ2 (the failure vocabulary), RQ18 (test and attack intents), RQ22 (invariants that run)"
    origin: >-
      James, 2026-10-13: "look in all relevant domains, including linguistics, communication, systems thinking, anything to
      do with traversal, davinci, all coding, developer domains, qa, qc, all of the domains that have ways to test code,
      applications, etc. recursive, deep, all time, meaning making, look at all the underlying prmitives, principles,
      invariants, and compare them across domains, to find, invent, and discover extensive tests, for all coding language,
      chuking, traversal between code, components, boundaries, anything online, make a huge list, for debugging, problem
      solving, quality checks, quality assurance, etc. for the test env, for the gates, the debugging system in repos, the
      diagnostic system and the intelligence system if applicable. i want nexus to learn. gates for everything to reduce
      workload from agents, checkpoints, and fault and fialure mode mapping, and diagnosing when there is a failure, tagging
      and updating the system each gate, gated, and tracked through the system."
    how_to_read: >-
      An entry is { id, name, family, domains, primitive, invariant, check, finds, how, stages, exists }.
      how — deterministic (a tool, no model) · model (needs a model's judgment; small first, RQ4's ladder) · person (only he
      can say). The point of the catalogue is that most entries are deterministic: every one a gate runs instead of an agent
      is work and tokens the agents do not spend.
      stages — where it runs: gate (a RAID/contract gate on one chunk, before it is accepted) · testenv (cos/testenv, a
      repo's tests in a guest) · torture (a torture-chamber station, adversarial) · debug (a repo's Debug tab, after a
      failure) · diagnostic (diagnostic/ and lib/diagnostic-engines.js, on a running system) · intelligence (intelligence/,
      over the ledgers, learning) · import (when a project is brought in — find what is already broken).
      Each check's failure is named in RQ2's vocabulary (or adds a class to it), so a failure is tagged, counted per model and
      per kind of chunk, and promoted to a .failure_mode node when it recurs (schema.failure_mode, FM4) — that is how Nexus
      learns from its gates.

  # ── The method: the same few primitives appear in every domain; each domain's way of testing one is a check ────────
  primitives:
    - id: boundary
      says: "where one thing ends and another begins: a module, a component, an API, a process, a trust zone, a chunk"
      invariant: "nothing crosses a boundary except through its declared door (a contract, an export, a route)"
      seen_as: "software: module interface, API, sandbox · systems thinking: system boundary · biology: cell membrane · law: jurisdiction · linguistics: word and sentence boundaries · security: trust boundary · Da Vinci: the edge (he drew the boundary as a gradient — sfumato — not a line: test the edge cases)"
    - id: flow
      says: "what moves: data, control, events, messages, money, attention"
      invariant: "what leaves one place arrives at the next, once, intact, in order — or the loss is said"
      seen_as: "software: data/control flow, events · systems thinking: stocks and flows · hydraulics (Da Vinci's water studies): continuity, turbulence · communication: Shannon's channel (sender, encoding, noise, receiver) · logistics: conservation"
    - id: state
      says: "what is remembered between moments"
      invariant: "every state is reachable on purpose, observable, and recoverable; no state is reachable that should not be"
      seen_as: "software: state machines, stores · physics: conservation · accounting: double entry (every change has two sides) · medicine: vital signs"
    - id: transformation
      says: "a step that turns an input into an output: a function, a gate, a build, a translation"
      invariant: "same input, same output (or the difference is declared); output satisfies its schema; input is not silently changed"
      seen_as: "mathematics: functions, morphisms · linguistics: translation (meaning preserved) · chemistry: reactions (mass balance) · manufacturing: a process step with its control chart"
    - id: invariant
      says: "what must stay true whatever happens"
      invariant: "it is written down, it is checked, and it is checked by something other than the thing that could break it"
      seen_as: "mathematics: loop invariants · law: constitutional rules · engineering: safety factors · Nexus: the axioms, a charter's always-true conditions"
    - id: feedback
      says: "an output that comes back as an input: retries, learning, control loops"
      invariant: "every loop has a bound, a damping, and a stop; it converges or says it does not"
      seen_as: "control theory: stability, gain · systems thinking: reinforcing and balancing loops · biology: homeostasis · economics: Goodhart (a measure that becomes a target)"
    - id: identity
      says: "what makes a thing itself: an id, a hash, a name, a signature"
      invariant: "one thing, one identity; the identity survives the thing being moved or copied; two things never share one"
      seen_as: "software: UUIDs, content hashes · law: provenance, chain of custody · linguistics: reference (what a word points at) · cryptography: signatures"
    - id: time
      says: "order and duration: before/after, timeouts, versions"
      invariant: "cause before effect; nothing waits forever; the order the system acts on is the order it records"
      seen_as: "distributed systems: logical clocks, happens-before · history: chronology and anachronism · music: tempo and sync · medicine: time to treatment"
    - id: cause
      says: "why something happened"
      invariant: "every effect names its cause, or says the cause is unknown; a hypothesis is not a cause until evidence separates it from the others"
      seen_as: "science: controlled experiments · medicine: differential diagnosis · engineering: fault trees, 5 whys, Ishikawa · law: burden of proof"
    - id: evidence
      says: "what shows a claim is true"
      invariant: "a claim of done, safe or fixed carries evidence a second party can re-run; a check that could not run is unknown, never pass"
      seen_as: "science: reproducibility · law: admissible evidence · accounting: audit trail · QA: acceptance criteria · Da Vinci: saper vedere — knowing how to see; 'experience never errs, it is only your judgments that err'"
    - id: meaning
      says: "what a name, a message or a document is taken to say"
      invariant: "one term, one meaning within a scope; what the code does matches what its name, its doc and its spec say"
      seen_as: "linguistics: semantics, pragmatics (what is meant vs said) · communication: grounding (shared understanding confirmed) · hermeneutics: the reading in context · Nexus: a phase's `james:` vs its `does:`"
    - id: composition
      says: "parts making a whole: components, chunks, modules, phases"
      invariant: "the whole's behaviour follows from the parts and their wiring; a part works alone and in place; nothing is in the whole that no part brought"
      seen_as: "software: integration, modularity · Da Vinci: connessione — everything connects to everything else · biology: organs and organism · music: harmony from voices"

  # ── The checks ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  checks:
    # 1. Parsing, structure, language — deterministic, cheapest, first in every gate
    - { id: CK-001, name: parses, family: structure, domains: [all languages], primitive: transformation, invariant: "the file is valid source in its language", check: "node --check / tsc --noEmit / python -m py_compile / the language's own parser", finds: "syntax errors before anything runs", how: deterministic, stages: [gate, import, diagnostic], exists: "diagnostic/nexus-diagnostic.js runAudit (node --check); cos/runtime/run.js syntaxCheck" }
    - { id: CK-002, name: requires resolve, family: structure, domains: [all languages], primitive: boundary, invariant: "every relative import points at a file that exists", check: "resolve each import against the tree (lib/component-store.js specsOf + _candidates)", finds: "broken imports — MASTERMIND had 143 on import (0.60.6)", how: deterministic, stages: [gate, import, debug], exists: "lib/component-store.js unresolved; cos/runtime/run.js resolveDeps" }
    - { id: CK-003, name: imported names exist, family: structure, domains: [js, ts, python], primitive: boundary, invariant: "a named import is exported by its target", check: "parse the target's exports; compare with the importer's names", finds: "invented or renamed symbols (the commonest small-model error)", how: deterministic, stages: [gate], exists: "lib/phase-plan.js checkChunk (export names present); lib/code-intel definition" }
    - { id: CK-004, name: no import cycles, family: structure, domains: [all languages], primitive: composition, invariant: "the require graph has no cycle, or each cycle is declared", check: "Tarjan SCC over the require graph", finds: "half-initialised modules, boot-order bugs", how: deterministic, stages: [import, diagnostic], exists: none }
    - { id: CK-005, name: dependency direction, family: structure, domains: [architecture], primitive: boundary, invariant: "lower layers never require higher ones (kernel → library → api → ui)", check: "layer of each file (registry card / path) vs the layer of what it requires", finds: "a UI file required by a library; a kernel importing a route", how: deterministic, stages: [gate, diagnostic], exists: "lib/component-boundary-check.js (partial)" }
    - { id: CK-006, name: npm dependency declared, family: structure, domains: [js], primitive: boundary, invariant: "every package imported is in package.json at a version", check: "component-store npm names vs package.json", finds: "works-on-my-machine imports", how: deterministic, stages: [import, gate], exists: "lib/project-decompose.js (npmVersions)" }
    - { id: CK-007, name: dead code, family: structure, domains: [all languages], primitive: composition, invariant: "every export has a consumer or is a declared entry point", check: "reverse the require graph; exports with no importer and no route/registry entry", finds: "abandoned modules, copies that drifted (MASTERMIND's unintegrated/)", how: deterministic, stages: [import, diagnostic], exists: "lib/registry-harness.js required-by (partial)" }
    - { id: CK-008, name: duplicate code, family: structure, domains: [all languages], primitive: identity, invariant: "one behaviour, one implementation", check: "hash normalised functions / chunks (component-store sha) across the tree", finds: "the same module in three versions (spatial-v2_0_0, v2_1_0, v2_2_0_1)", how: deterministic, stages: [import, diagnostic], exists: "lib/component-store.js sha256 (per file)" }
    - { id: CK-009, name: type agreement, family: structure, domains: [ts, js with JSDoc, python with hints], primitive: boundary, invariant: "callers pass what callees declare", check: "tsc --checkJs / mypy where configured; else arity and shape of call sites vs signature", finds: "wrong argument shapes across a boundary", how: deterministic, stages: [gate, testenv], exists: none }
    - { id: CK-010, name: complexity bound, family: structure, domains: [all languages], primitive: transformation, invariant: "a function stays within a cyclomatic and length budget unless it says why", check: "count branches and lines per function", finds: "functions too large for a small model to edit safely", how: deterministic, stages: [gate, import], exists: none }
    - { id: CK-011, name: chunk is self-contained, family: chunking, domains: [Nexus], primitive: boundary, invariant: "a chunk names every symbol it uses from outside it, and the names resolve", check: "free identifiers of the chunk vs its imports + the registry card's exports", finds: "chunks that only make sense with another chunk in view", how: deterministic, stages: [gate], exists: "lib/build-context.js (what did not fit)" }
    - { id: CK-012, name: chunk cut at a symbol, family: chunking, domains: [Nexus], primitive: boundary, invariant: "a chunk starts and ends at a symbol boundary (function, class, block)", check: "the chunk's first and last lines are a whole declaration (parser ranges)", finds: "chunks cut mid-function", how: deterministic, stages: [gate, import], exists: "lib/chunker structuralProfile, detectSubBoundaries" }
    - { id: CK-013, name: chunk fits the model, family: chunking, domains: [Nexus], primitive: flow, invariant: "the chunk plus its context fits the chosen model's window with room for the answer", check: "token estimate vs the rung's window (pipeline-routing ladder)", finds: "truncated replies, empty replies", how: deterministic, stages: [gate], exists: "lib/pipeline-routing.js (truncated class)" }
    - { id: CK-014, name: anchor still matches, family: chunking, domains: [Nexus], primitive: identity, invariant: "the lines a chunk edits are the lines it was planned against (hash)", check: "re-hash the anchor range before the edit", finds: "edits landing on code that moved", how: deterministic, stages: [gate], exists: "lib/repo-inject.js appliedSha256 (after); RQ10 (before)" }
    - { id: CK-015, name: edit within scope, family: chunking, domains: [Nexus], primitive: boundary, invariant: "a chunk changes only the files and lines its contract block declares", check: "diff paths and hunks vs the block's files/lines", finds: "undeclared edits, collateral damage", how: deterministic, stages: [gate], exists: "RQ10 (reconcile)" }
    - { id: CK-016, name: output is not a repeat, family: chunking, domains: [Nexus], primitive: feedback, invariant: "a retry's output differs from the failed one", check: "similarity of the new output to the previous attempt (lib/semantic-variant similarity)", finds: "a model stuck in a loop", how: deterministic, stages: [gate], exists: "lib/semantic-variant.js similarity" }

    # 2. Behaviour — does it do what it says
    - { id: CK-020, name: tests pass, family: behaviour, domains: [all], primitive: evidence, invariant: "the repo's own tests pass after the change as they did before", check: "run the tests in cos/testenv; compare with the baseline run", finds: "regressions", how: deterministic, stages: [testenv, gate], exists: "cos/testenv; idearium/repo/proof-run.js kind tests" }
    - { id: CK-021, name: differential (before/after), family: behaviour, domains: [all], primitive: evidence, invariant: "a test that failed before the change is not counted as the change's failure, and one that passed must still pass", check: "run the suite on the baseline and the changed branch; diff verdicts", finds: "regressions vs old failures", how: deterministic, stages: [testenv], exists: "cos/playground/compare.js CompareEngine" }
    - { id: CK-022, name: property-based, family: behaviour, domains: [mathematics, all languages], primitive: invariant, invariant: "a stated property holds for generated inputs, not only the examples", check: "generate inputs (fast-check / hypothesis style), shrink failures", finds: "edge cases nobody wrote down", how: deterministic, stages: [testenv, torture], exists: none }
    - { id: CK-023, name: metamorphic, family: behaviour, domains: [science, ML testing], primitive: transformation, invariant: "related inputs give related outputs (sort(x) == sort(shuffle(x)))", check: "apply a transformation with a known effect; compare outputs", finds: "bugs where there is no oracle for the right answer", how: deterministic, stages: [testenv, torture], exists: none }
    - { id: CK-024, name: golden / snapshot, family: behaviour, domains: [all], primitive: identity, invariant: "a known input still gives the recorded output, or the change is approved", check: "compare with a stored output", finds: "unintended output changes", how: deterministic, stages: [testenv], exists: "cos/playground/compare.js golden branch" }
    - { id: CK-025, name: mutation, family: behaviour, domains: [software testing], primitive: evidence, invariant: "the tests fail when the code is broken", check: "flip an operator / condition / constant; run the tests; survivors are untested behaviour", finds: "tests that test nothing", how: deterministic, stages: [torture], exists: none }
    - { id: CK-026, name: contract (consumer-driven), family: behaviour, domains: [APIs, microservices], primitive: boundary, invariant: "a provider still answers what its consumers rely on", check: "replay each consumer's recorded requests against the provider; compare shape", finds: "breaking API changes", how: deterministic, stages: [gate, testenv], exists: "lib/route-contract-check.js; intelligence/cfr/contract-verifier.js" }
    - { id: CK-027, name: acceptance conditions met, family: behaviour, domains: [QA], primitive: evidence, invariant: "every condition of the contract is met by evidence, not by the agent's report", check: "run each condition's check kind (file · command · tests · page)", finds: "'done' that is not done", how: deterministic, stages: [gate], exists: "idearium/repo/proof-run.js; lib/end-state.js" }
    - { id: CK-028, name: boot probe, family: behaviour, domains: [services, apps], primitive: state, invariant: "the app starts, listens and answers its health route", check: "start, wait for listen, GET /health, stop", finds: "apps that do not start", how: deterministic, stages: [testenv, import], exists: "cos/runtime/run.js bootProbe" }
    - { id: CK-029, name: idempotency, family: behaviour, domains: [distributed systems, payments], primitive: state, invariant: "doing it twice is the same as doing it once", check: "replay the same request/event twice; compare state", finds: "double writes, double sends", how: deterministic, stages: [torture, testenv], exists: none }
    - { id: CK-030, name: round-trip, family: behaviour, domains: [serialization, linguistics (back-translation)], primitive: transformation, invariant: "decode(encode(x)) == x; export → import is lossless", check: "round-trip every format the system writes", finds: "lossy save/load (a .gig, a node file, a contract)", how: deterministic, stages: [gate, testenv], exists: "clear-glass/test/gig-file.test.js (one format)" }

    # 3. Runtime, concurrency, distributed — what happens when things go wrong at once
    - { id: CK-040, name: fault injection, family: runtime, domains: [chaos engineering, aviation], primitive: cause, invariant: "a dependency failing produces a named, handled failure, never a hang or a silent wrong answer", check: "kill / delay / error each dependency in turn", finds: "missing error paths", how: deterministic, stages: [torture, testenv], exists: "cos/spec/torture-chamber.spec (station, unbuilt)" }
    - { id: CK-041, name: timeouts bounded, family: runtime, domains: [distributed systems], primitive: time, invariant: "every wait has a limit and says what it waited for", check: "find network/IPC calls without a timeout (static) and stall them (dynamic)", finds: "hangs", how: deterministic, stages: [gate, diagnostic], exists: none }
    - { id: CK-042, name: races, family: runtime, domains: [concurrency], primitive: time, invariant: "the result does not depend on scheduling", check: "run concurrent operations in shuffled orders; compare end state", finds: "lost updates, check-then-act bugs", how: deterministic, stages: [torture], exists: none }
    - { id: CK-043, name: crash consistency, family: runtime, domains: [databases, file systems], primitive: state, invariant: "a crash at any point leaves state readable and recoverable", check: "kill the process at each write; restart; verify", finds: "half-written files (write without tmp + rename)", how: deterministic, stages: [torture], exists: "atomic writes in lib (convention, not a check)" }
    - { id: CK-044, name: retry has a bound and a backoff, family: runtime, domains: [control theory], primitive: feedback, invariant: "retries stop, back off, and do not amplify load", check: "static: loops around calls without a cap; dynamic: count retries under failure", finds: "retry storms", how: deterministic, stages: [gate, diagnostic], exists: "guardian/lib/job-retry.js (one place)" }
    - { id: CK-045, name: backpressure, family: runtime, domains: [stream processing, hydraulics], primitive: flow, invariant: "a slow consumer slows the producer or is told; queues are bounded", check: "flood the input; watch queue length and memory", finds: "unbounded queues, OOM (the idearium heap crash)", how: deterministic, stages: [torture, diagnostic], exists: "lib/diagnostic-engines.js memory_pressure" }
    - { id: CK-046, name: memory and handle leaks, family: runtime, domains: [operations], primitive: state, invariant: "resident memory and open handles return to baseline after work", check: "soak run; sample heap and handles", finds: "leaks", how: deterministic, stages: [torture, diagnostic], exists: "clear-glass/src/diagnostic/process-metrics.js" }
    - { id: CK-047, name: clock and ordering, family: runtime, domains: [distributed systems, history], primitive: time, invariant: "events are ordered by logical time, and clock jumps do not reorder them", check: "skew the clock; verify ledger order", finds: "ordering by wall clock", how: deterministic, stages: [torture], exists: "AXIOMS §3.2 (eventTs, a rule not a check)" }
    - { id: CK-048, name: partial failure across systems, family: runtime, domains: [distributed systems], primitive: composition, invariant: "a request that fails halfway is completed, compensated or marked — never half-applied silently", check: "fail the second of two systems mid-handoff", finds: "orphaned state (a job queued with no tab)", how: deterministic, stages: [torture], exists: "cos/archetype/nexus-system/lib/handoff.js recover (template)" }

    # 4. Security — adversarial
    - { id: CK-060, name: secrets in code and logs, family: security, domains: [security], primitive: boundary, invariant: "no credential is written to source, a log, a node or a .input", check: "entropy + pattern scan of files and writes", finds: "leaked keys", how: deterministic, stages: [gate, import, diagnostic], exists: none }
    - { id: CK-061, name: path traversal, family: security, domains: [security], primitive: boundary, invariant: "a path from outside cannot leave its root", check: "feed ../, absolute, encoded and symlink paths to every file-taking route", finds: "writes outside the repo", how: deterministic, stages: [torture, gate], exists: "lib/zip-ingest.js _safeRelPath; diagnostic path_traversal_regression" }
    - { id: CK-062, name: injection, family: security, domains: [security], primitive: boundary, invariant: "input is data, never code: shell, SQL, HTML, prompt", check: "taint from inputs to exec/eval/innerHTML/shell and to prompts", finds: "command injection, XSS, prompt injection", how: deterministic, stages: [gate, torture], exists: none }
    - { id: CK-063, name: prompt injection resistance, family: security, domains: [LLM security], primitive: boundary, invariant: "text read from a page, a file or another agent cannot change what an agent is allowed to do", check: "seed instructions in retrieved content; verify no tool call follows them", finds: "agents steered by data", how: deterministic, stages: [torture], exists: none }
    - { id: CK-064, name: dependency vulnerabilities and licences, family: security, domains: [supply chain], primitive: identity, invariant: "no dependency with a known critical vulnerability or an incompatible licence", check: "audit the lockfile (offline database when available)", finds: "known-bad packages", how: deterministic, stages: [import, gate], exists: none }
    - { id: CK-065, name: least privilege, family: security, domains: [security, law], primitive: boundary, invariant: "a component holds only the capabilities its work needs", check: "compare the routes/files/network a component touches with what its registry entry declares", finds: "over-broad access", how: deterministic, stages: [diagnostic], exists: "cos/foundation/axioms.js (COS compartment network/fs)" }
    - { id: CK-066, name: default off, family: security, domains: [security (FPF threat model)], primitive: state, invariant: "no new network surface is on by default; no update can turn one on remotely", check: "boot a fresh install; list listening sockets and enabled features", finds: "exposure for at-risk users", how: deterministic, stages: [testenv], exists: "docs/nexus-uri-clearglass-mesh-integration.spec default_off, no_remote_flip (rules)" }

    # 5. Interface, communication, language
    - { id: CK-080, name: every action reachable, family: interface, domains: [UX, accessibility], primitive: flow, invariant: "every capability has a screen, a command and a route (backend → API → command → UI)", check: "registry entries vs routes vs command rows vs UI handlers", finds: "capabilities only one door reaches", how: deterministic, stages: [gate, diagnostic], exists: "tests/modules/test-cli-route-commands.test.js (partial)" }
    - { id: CK-081, name: accessible, family: interface, domains: [accessibility], primitive: meaning, invariant: "every control has a name, is reachable by keyboard, and has contrast ≥ 4.5:1", check: "walk the DOM in Clear Glass (glass.js): roles, names, tab order, computed contrast", finds: "unlabelled buttons, keyboard traps", how: deterministic, stages: [testenv], exists: none }
    - { id: CK-082, name: layout holds, family: interface, domains: [visual QA], primitive: boundary, invariant: "no overflow, overlap or clipped text at the supported sizes", check: "render at 360/768/1280/1920 widths in Clear Glass; detect overflow and overlap", finds: "broken layouts", how: deterministic, stages: [testenv], exists: "clear-glass screen QA (partial)" }
    - { id: CK-083, name: error messages are actionable, family: communication, domains: [communication, UX writing], primitive: meaning, invariant: "every error says what failed, why, and what to do next", check: "collect error strings; flag those without a cause or a next step", finds: "'something went wrong'", how: model, stages: [gate, diagnostic], exists: none }
    - { id: CK-084, name: one term one meaning, family: language, domains: [linguistics, terminology management], primitive: meaning, invariant: "a term means one thing in a scope; one thing has one name", check: "extract identifiers and doc terms; cluster synonyms and homonyms (synthesis used for two different things)", finds: "two systems meaning different things by one word", how: deterministic, stages: [diagnostic, import], exists: none }
    - { id: CK-085, name: code says what its name says, family: language, domains: [linguistics, semantics], primitive: meaning, invariant: "a function's name, its doc and its behaviour agree", check: "compare the name/doc with the behaviour summary of the body", finds: "misleading names, stale comments", how: model, stages: [gate, debug], exists: none }
    - { id: CK-086, name: spec matches code, family: language, domains: [hermeneutics, QA], primitive: meaning, invariant: "every claim in a spec has code, every behaviour in code has a claim, or the drift is written", check: "spec claims (paths, names, routes) vs the tree; routes in code vs routes in specs", finds: "specs describing code that is not there", how: deterministic, stages: [diagnostic, import], exists: "loom spec-map, wiring-gaps; idearium/repo/living-spec.js (drift)" }
    - { id: CK-087, name: grounding of a request, family: communication, domains: [conversation analysis, communication], primitive: meaning, invariant: "before work starts, the request is restated and confirmed; unknowns are asked, not assumed", check: "the contract's restatement + its open questions; no block without a confirmed need", finds: "building the wrong thing", how: person, stages: [gate], exists: "lib/context-prereqs.js (asks what is missing)" }
    - { id: CK-088, name: readable, family: language, domains: [linguistics, plain language], primitive: meaning, invariant: "docs and messages a person reads are short sentences in plain words", check: "sentence length, jargon density, passive voice (readability scores)", finds: "text he has to decode", how: deterministic, stages: [gate], exists: none }

    # 6. Systems thinking, structure of the whole
    - { id: CK-100, name: every component has a wire, family: systems, domains: [systems thinking, graph theory], primitive: composition, invariant: "no component is an island: each has at least one real in- or out-edge", check: "loom registry: components with no wires", finds: "orphans the system cannot reason about", how: deterministic, stages: [diagnostic], exists: "diagnostic/wire-integrity.js; diagnostic orphaned_hook" }
    - { id: CK-101, name: single points of failure, family: systems, domains: [reliability engineering], primitive: composition, invariant: "losing any one component degrades named things, never everything silently", check: "articulation points of the dependency graph; the boot order's critical path", finds: "one process whose death stops all", how: deterministic, stages: [diagnostic], exists: none }
